<!-- v2 (2026-11-16): rewritten for the rebuilt tool. The opening paragraph
     is the prose moved word for word from the 1.x screen header. -->
<h3 class="help first">What this tool does</h3>
<p class="help">Manage the AcoustID fingerprinting lifecycle. Submit unknown tracks to the global database, or check previously submitted tracks to resolve and finalize their identifiers.</p>

<p class="help">AcoustID is a free, shared database that recognises a recording by how it sounds (its "fingerprint"). The Intelli-Tagger looks up every track. When AcoustID doesn't know a track yet, the track is added to a waiting list here. Submitting is optional, and it helps everyone who uses AcoustID.</p>

<h3>1. Submit new fingerprints</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Sends each waiting track's fingerprint to AcoustID, with its title, artist, album, release year and MusicBrainz recording ID when MetaForge has them.</li>
    <li>Needs two keys in <strong>Settings &gt; Configuration &amp; keys</strong>: the AcoustID application key and your own AcoustID user key (shown at acoustid.org once you're signed in).</li>
    <li>A track that can't be sent stays in the list for next time.</li>
</ul>

<h3>2. Collect AcoustIDs</h3>
<ul>
    <li>AcoustID adds submissions in the background. This step asks AcoustID which of your submissions are done, and collects their AcoustIDs.</li>
    <li>A track MetaForge already knows gets its AcoustID in the file's tag and in the database.</li>
    <li>A file whose album hasn't been through the Intelli-Tagger yet is left alone. Its submission still counts: the Intelli-Tagger finds the AcoustID itself when you process that album.</li>
    <li>Tracks still being processed stay in the list. Check again later.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Stopping and leaving</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Stop</strong> ends the run after the current track. Everything done so far is kept, and the rest stays in the list.</li>
    <li>If you switch tools during a run, MetaForge asks first.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Where the lists are kept</h3>
<p>In the <code>data\acoustid</code> folder: <code>pending_acoustid.txt</code> (waiting to be submitted), <code>submission_history.txt</code> (waiting for an AcoustID), <code>submission_ids.json</code> (AcoustID's number for each submission) and <code>not_found.txt</code> (files that were moved or renamed before they could be handled).</p>
<!-- --- END OF FILE help.mfi --- -->
